# Regenerable from storage at any time, and these belong in the bucket, not the repo.
webp-fix/

# Raw authored room shells. The shell ships through a two-step pipeline — compress-room-glb.mjs then
# set-shell-blend-modes.mjs — and only the OUTPUT belongs in the bundle: the authored export is ~9 MB
# of 4K texture payload, and a shell committed without the blend-mode pass ships walls that never fade.
# An allowlist rather than a per-file rule, so a re-export under any name stays out by default.
src/assets/models/room/*.glb
!src/assets/models/room/virtualroom_empty.glb
# The authoring source now lives beside its output (room.blend, ~132 MB, plus the .blend1 Blender writes on every save) and the AO bake drops room_ao.png next to whatever .blend is open. None of it belongs in git: the .blend is the size of the whole repo several times over, and room_ao.png is already packed inside the .blend AND baked into the shipped GLB, so committing it stores a third copy that nothing reads.
src/assets/models/room/*.blend
src/assets/models/room/*.blend[0-9]
src/assets/models/room/room_ao.png

